# Build context, trimmed to what the images read (`D10-114`).
#
# There was no such file, so `docker build .` sent the whole repository — including
# `venv/`, every `node_modules/` and the running tree's `__pycache__` — to the
# daemon, and the `COPY` of `backend/migrations` imported whatever byte-compiled
# files happened to be lying in the developer's checkout. An image that depends on
# which commands were run before it was built is not the artifact CI signs off on.
#
# Nothing needed by a `COPY` or a `pip install` is listed here: `backend/app`,
# `backend/requirements*.txt`, `backend/alembic.ini` and `backend/migrations` are
# all still in context, and anything a build genuinely needs that is missing would
# fail the build loudly rather than silently ship a thinner image.

**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# The virtualenv, the JavaScript dependency trees and the two frontend sources:
# no Dockerfile here copies from any of them, and between them they are the bulk
# of the context.
venv/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
demo/frontend/node_modules/
demo/frontend/.next/
node_modules/

# VCS and agent scratch space, never useful inside an image.
.git/
.gitattributes
.agent-cache/
.env
!.env.example
